/-!
# Atlas V-02 (B, null frames): lowered connection, Koszul formula, frame Riemann and Weyl components

Four-dimensional specialisation of `FrameConn` to frames whose (complex-bilinear) Gram matrix is V-01's constant
`etaNull` (`g(l,n) = −1`, `g(m,m̄) = 1`, signature `(−,+,+,+)`); index order `0 = l, 1 = n, 2 = m, 3 = m̄`.
`NullFrameData` adds only this kinematic normalisation to `FrameData` (no curvature, NP or field equation).
Class B definitions:

* `omL C A B = Σ_K η_{CK} Ω_A^K_B = g(e_C, ∇_{e_A} e_B)` and `cL C A B = Σ_K η_{CK} c^K_{AB} = g(e_C, [e_A, e_B])`;
* `ccontr4 T x u v w z = Σ T_{abcd} u^a v^b w^c z^d` (complex-multilinear, no conjugation);
* `riemFL I J A B = Σ_K η_{IK} (Rfr A B)^K_J` (frame curvature with the first index lowered);
* `ricF A B = Ric(e_A, e_B)`, `weylF I J A B = C(e_I, e_J, e_A, e_B)`, `FfrF A B = F(e_A, e_B)`.

