/-!
# Atlas V-02 (C, part 3): the Kerr–Newman connection components `omL` (all 24) via the Koszul formula

`omL C A B = g(e_C, ∇_{e_A} e_B)` of V-01's Kinnersley frame, obtained from the **proved** Koszul formula
(`NullFrameData.omL_koszul`, constant Gram matrix) and the computed commutator coefficients `cL`
(`KNComm.lean`). No Christoffel table is used; no value is assumed. Every real `M, a, Q`; on IV's `domReg`.
The table is antisymmetric in `C ↔ B` (`omL_antisymm`), so the 24 entries with `C < B` determine all 64.
-/

open Real Complex
open scoped ComplexConjugate
open ExactVacuumAtlas.EinsteinMaxwell.KN (Sig Del gKN domReg domReg_S domReg_D domReg_s)

